<title>ITALY: Gross yields rise at Italian Btp bond auction.</title>
<headline>Gross yields rise at Italian Btp bond auction.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Auction results for a fifth tranche of 2.0 trillion lire worth of three-year Italian Treasury fixed rate bonds (Btp) with a 6.00 pct coupon, and a third tranche of 1.5 trillion lire of five-year Btps carrying a 6.25 pct coupon.</p>
<p>		  Feb 15, 2000   pvs	March 1, 2002   pvs</p>
<p> Net Yield	 6.26 pct    5.80	  6.35 pct     5.94</p>
<p> Gross Yield     7.04 pct    6.58	  7.22 pct     6.80</p>
<p> Assigned price 97.55	 98.70	 96.50	  98.15</p>
<p> Bids	     4.733 trln lire	   2.757 trln lire</p>
<p> Assigned	 2.000 trln lire	   1.500 trln lire</p>
<p>Note - The comparisons are with a previous auction on February 28 of a third tranche of the 3-year paper and a first tranche of five-year BTPs.</p>
</text>
